error[ffi_declared_two_ways]: `twice` is declared `double (double)` in `fixedbugs-555-double.h` line 3 and `long long (long long)` in `fixedbugs-555-long.h` line 2: two groups bind one C function two ways, and the linker joins both to one symbol
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2136-a-value-only-the-probe-sees-is-told-beside-a-function-two-groups-bind-two-ways.hero:13:14
     |
  13 |     function twice(x: f64) -> f64  #~ ffi_declared_two_ways
     |              ^^^^^
  note: the other module's group is at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs555/long_twice.hero:5
  note: each module's unit reads its own headers, so both compile, and C then reaches one `twice` through two types, reading what it is given and what it returns as the other's (C11 6.2.7): bind `twice` in both modules from the header that declares it as it is defined, or from one module, whose unit reads both headers, where clang refuses the two declarations together

error[ffi_constant_type]: `K_DIV` in `fixedbugs-2128-values.h` cannot be declared `i64`: clang refuses the header's value at line 4: its expression holds an operation C leaves undefined for the operands it is given, and the program's own unit, built with clang's checks for an overflow, a shift, a division by zero and a float out of an integer's range, traps where it reads it
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2136-a-value-only-the-probe-sees-is-told-beside-a-function-two-groups-bind-two-ways.hero:16:5
     |
  16 |     constant K_DIV: i64  #~ ffi_constant_type
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: `fixedbugs-2128-values.h` line 4 reads `#define K_DIV ((-2147483647 - 1) / -1)`
  note: an operation C leaves undefined gives no value: wherever C computes it, a program reading `K_DIV` reads whatever the machine held. A group's `constant` is the value C computes from the header (§ 13): correct the value there, or bind a constant whose value C defines
